      "costUsd": 0.008291000000000001,
      "pronunciationText": "Last video stopped at one over x, where the power rule would divide by zero. Here's a rate like that. A fundraiser's donations slow down. On day t, they come in at a thousand over t dollars a day. So the total raised has gradient a thousand over t. The same term sits in this question: two e to the three x, plus four over x. The first term is done: two thirds e to the three x. The second is still waiting. So which curve has a gradient of one over x? And why will the answer need the absolute value of x, often read as mod x?"
    },
    {
