      "possibleRetry": false,
      "inputTokens": 98,
      "outputTokens": 718,
      "costUsd": 0.006510999999999999,
      "pronunciationText": "Put the two pieces together. For positive x we have the natural log of x, and for negative x, the natural log of minus x. Both are the natural log of mod x. Mod x is the size of x without its sign. Now watch the gradient as a point moves along each piece. On both sides, it traces one over x exactly. So the integral of one over x is the natural log of mod x, plus C, for x not equal to zero."
    },
    {
      "id": "scene-05",
      "changed": true,
      "audio": "public/audio/math-a12-i04/scene-05.wav",
