      "loggedRequestAttempts": 1,
      "possibleRetry": false,
      "inputTokens": 119,
      "outputTokens": 809,
      "costUsd": 0.0073405,
      "pronunciationText": "Notice the gap at zero. One over x isn't defined there, and mod x doesn't fill the gap. So this primitive is two separate pieces. Slide the right piece up, and its gradients don't change. Slide the left piece down, and the same is true. Nothing joins the pieces across zero, so each one can have its own constant. Differentiate any of these curves, and you get one over x on each piece. In a question, you work on one piece at a time, so you write the natural log of mod x, plus C."
    },
