      "possibleRetry": false,
      "inputTokens": 99,
      "outputTokens": 770,
      "costUsd": 0.0069795000000000005,
      "pronunciationText": "Back to the waiting term. Four over x is four times one over x, so its integral is four times the natural log of mod x. Add the first term, and one constant for the whole answer. That's two thirds e to the three x, plus four times the natural log of mod x, plus C, for x not equal to zero. Differentiate back to check. Two thirds times three gives two e to the three x, and four over x comes back."
