      "inputTokens": 155,
      "outputTokens": 1096,
      "costUsd": 0.009941499999999999,
      "pronunciationText": "Now a reciprocal with an inside. Find the integral of one over two x minus three. Try the natural log of mod two x minus three. By the chain rule, its derivative is two over two x minus three, twice what we want. On the graph, the log curve is squashed sideways by a factor of two, then slid along. The slide changes no slopes, but the squash doubles every one. It's the same cause as before, so divide by the inner rate. The answer is a half, times the natural log of mod two x minus three, plus C. The gap moves too. Two x minus three is zero at x equals three over two, so the answer works on either side of three over two, but not across it."
    },
