      "inputTokens": 142,
      "outputTokens": 1017,
      "costUsd": 0.009224,
      "pronunciationText": "What if the top isn't just ay number? Find the integral of two x over x squared plus four. Look at the bottom. Its derivative is two x, which is exactly the top. By the chain rule, the natural log of mod f has derivative f prime over f. So this integral is the natural log of mod x squared plus four, plus C. Here, x squared plus four is at least four, so it's always positive. The absolute value can go, and the answer works for every x. But if the bottom were x squared minus four, it would change sign, so you'd keep the absolute value, with gaps at x equals two and minus two."
    },
