      "pronunciationText": "The bottom, three x plus one, has derivative three, and six is two times three. So the answer is two times the natural log of mod three x plus one, plus C. Differentiate back: two times three, over three x plus one, gives six over three x plus one. It's valid for x not equal to minus one third, on either side of it. Six times the log is wrong. It forgets to divide by the inner three."
